================================================================================
AGPL § 13 — Network use
================================================================================

If you run a modified version of this program on a server, AGPL § 13
requires you to offer the source code to users interacting with that
server over a network. The recommended way is to display a "Source" link
in the user-facing UI of any service that wraps `slicer-cli`. The Helio
closed apps (commercial Tauri shell + cloud server) wrap `slicer-cli`
via subprocess invocation only — they do NOT link the AGPL code, so
their UI is not bound by AGPL § 13. Direct consumers of `slicer-cli`
(for example, third-party services) ARE bound by § 13 and must offer
the source.
